{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992868-help-create-new-england-small-town","id":992868,"title":"Help create New England small town","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-25T03:11:09-07:00","id":992868,"title":"Help create New England small town","content":"So I preper to run zombies game on this Saturday. I have more or less plot, talked about zombies rules in 2E before. What I need are small details - general map, maybe what can be found in particular buildings, this kind of thing. As I'm from Europe ( Poland, to be precise ) I cannot find any 'classical' resources - If you could help me make this setting to be 'horror movie America', with some maps or pointing stuff to be found in territory.<br /> <br /> Town is called to be Somewhere - yes, for obvious pun like 'Somewhere in USA'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's 'classical' small town in New England, surround by great forests, at least one hour of drive from highway. Mostly whites in demographics, protestant church goers.<br /> <br /> So point me what I should have in it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:12:30-07:00","id":993063,"title":"","content":"The modern small town in New England is dominated by a city center or &quot;node&quot; where most of the hustle and bustle of the city takes place. First, you need a church. Probably several. Small New England towns propped up mostly around the churchgoing communities in the late 18th century and since then. The largest church is very often at the actual center of town or near the town center. Beyond that, you need a school, probably one that covers first grade through high school (approximately ages 6 to 18), where the locals send their children. Because it's a small town, there isn't much choice in public education and everyone goes to the same school. There may be a private school (probably associated with the church I mentioned earlier) in addition to the public school. Decide how small your town is going to be and then based on the size decide whether or not it will have a supermarket in it. This is another congregation point in towns that are large enough to have supermarkets. There will also most likely be places for youth to hang out: most likely a movie theater, a park, a late-night joint (think Denny's or IHOP).<br /> <br /> Do you have more details on what kind of town it is? It'll most likely be filled with either colonial style homes or brownstones, mostly of the older variety. If you can tell me more about the kind of town you're thinking of I can try to think of real world examples.<br /> <br /> (Source for all of this: lived in small town, New England <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:11:44-07:00","id":993595,"title":"","content":"Very informative, Kvark, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:51:48-07:00","id":993647,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <b>Kvark</b>! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992868-help-create-new-england-small-town?p=993063#post993063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have more details on what kind of town it is? It'll most likely be filled with either colonial style homes or brownstones, mostly of the older variety. If you can tell me more about the kind of town you're thinking of I can try to think of real world examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I do not have more details - I wanted this to be vauge as it's one-shot game. If I would go for any real world examples it would be... TV series towns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:28:37-07:00","id":993666,"title":"","content":"Yeah if I were you I would focus a lot on the school. Schools in those towns tend not only to be community centers, they also serve as emergency service locations. In small towns the school will often include things like natural disaster shelter, emergency medical supplies, and a large cache of canned food and water. Because most small towns don't have a hospital if a tragedy occurs they may set up trauma relief centers in the school. If I were playing in a zombie game, it's the place I'd want to go. Supermarkets might be great for supplies but schools usually have enough food on hand to feed a few hundred people for a few days as well as emergency medical equipment. <br /> <br /> If it's a really small town I would say there shouldn't be a hospital, or the nearest hospital should be some drive away (say 20 minutes or so). There is probably going to be a 24 hour clinic in the town that also serves as a makeshift emergency room that has hospital admitting privileges (serious cases get stabilized and sent to the nearby hospital ASAP).<br /> <br /> Other typical fixings of a small town in New England include the town liquor store, the town park, and maybe a street (you can make one up) that has a few different bars and nightlife on it. This street tends to be where the action is after-hours.<br /> <br /> I'll punch out more as I think of it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:12:21-07:00","id":993693,"title":"","content":"Arkham is THE New England horror town, I found a link to an easy to use map of it.<br /> <br /> If you don't want a Lovecraftian feel, just use the map as a template, move, adjust, add, remove, and rename landmarks as you choose, and rename the town.<br /> <br /> Still Arkham is basically designed as the perfect New England horror town. Not far from Salem and other good horror locations as well. Its a fictional town, but I THINK its public domain now, I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cthulhufiles.com/images/arkham.gif\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cthulhufiles.com/images/arkham.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cthulhufiles.com/images/arkham.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.cthulhufiles.com/images/arkham.gif </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T10:27:51-08:00","id":1007756,"title":"","content":"I found that fan made maps based from Stephen King's stories are great for general 'New England small town' feel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/stephenking/images/d/dc/Map_of_Derry.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/618?cb=20130810013403\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/stephenking/images/c/ca/Chester-MillsLarge900x666.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/640?cb=20100105212930\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T15:33:15-08:00","id":1007860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992868-help-create-new-england-small-town?p=993647#post993647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, <b>Kvark</b>!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No. I do not have more details - I wanted this to be vauge as it's one-shot game. If I would go for any real world examples it would be... TV series towns?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're looking for a T.V show maybe the series Haven","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1